course: dictionary
lesson: 12437
title: The decimeter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A decimeter is a unit of length. It is a way to measure how long something is, such as a pencil or a shelf. A meter is split into ten equal parts, and each part is one decimeter.
explain: One decimeter is 10 centimeters, so 1 dm = 10 cm. A meter is 10 decimeters, so 1 m = 10 dm. Each metric unit is 10 times bigger than the one before it, which makes the numbers easy to change.
explain: «The shelf is 3 decimeters long.» That is the same as 30 centimeters. When you have no ruler, picture the width of a grown-up's hand: that is about one decimeter.
fact: A decimeter is a unit of length.
fact: 1 decimeter = 10 centimeters, and 10 decimeters = 1 meter.
fact: «The pencil is 2 decimeters long.» That is 20 centimeters.
fact: A decimeter is about the width of a grown-up's hand.
fact: In British English the word is spelled decimetre, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «The book is 2 decimeters wide.» How many centimeters is that? | 10 | 2 | 200 | *20
exercise: «The table is 1 meter long.» How many decimeters is that? | 100 | *10 | 1 | 5
exercise: What is a decimeter about the width of? | *A grown-up's hand | A grown-up's car | A door | A football
test: «Ella's ribbon is 4 decimeters long.» How many centimeters is the ribbon? | 4 | 14 | 400 | *40
test: Which length is the same as 1 decimeter? | 5 centimeters | *10 centimeters | 1 centimeter | 100 centimeters
exam: «The rope is 3 decimeters long, and Sam cuts off 1 decimeter.» How many centimeters of rope are left? | *20 | 30 | 2 | 10
